(GRM-23: string ::= '"' ... '"' - "a string literal is data, never a
 name" is the production's own annotation. Using a double-quoted string
 where a name is expected is a compile error, and the compiler's own
 diagnostic says exactly that (cross-ref Names and Strings, LANGUAGE.md
 645-670, which motivated the 0.3.0 split between string literals and
 identifiers this production records).
 (Compile-error claim: not assertable from a generated leaf.)
